{
  "description": "Formulate a MILP for integrated train rescheduling and speed management under partial segment blockage. Sets: trains i in I, segments s in S, time periods t in T. Parameters: original departure/arrival times a_i^orig, d_i^orig, travel time on segment s for train i at speed level k: tau_{i,s,k}, energy consumption e_{i,s,k}, blockage window [t_start_s, t_end_s] on segment s, capacity of segment per direction cap_s. Binary x_{i,s,k} = 1 if train i uses speed level k on segment s. Binary y_{i,s}=1 if train i uses opposite track (reroute) on segment s. Continuous arrival time A_{i,s}, departure time D_{i,s}. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay sum_i (A_{i,last}-a_i^orig) and total energy sum_{i,s,k} e_{i,s,k} x_{i,s,k}. Constraints: each train chooses exactly one speed level per segment sum_k x_{i,s,k}=1. Timing: D_{i,s}=A_{i,s}+ sum_k tau_{i,s,k} x_{i,s,k}. Travel continuity: A_{i,next(s)} >= D_{i,s}+ headway_{i,i',s} * z_{i,i',s} where z binary for conflict. Blockage: if segment s blocked in window, then D_{i,s} <= t_start_s or A_{i,s} >= t_end_s unless reroute y_{i,s}=1. Reroute capacity: sum_i y_{i,s} <= cap_s. Conflict on shared track: for any two trains i,i' using same direction or opposite on same segment, enforce ordering via binary o_{i,i',s}: A_{i',s} >= D_{i,s} - M(1-o_{i,i',s}) and A_{i,s} >= D_{i',s} - M o_{i,i',s}. Energy calculation: total energy = sum_{i,s,k} e_{i,s,k} x_{i,s,k}. Variables bounds and domains defined."
}

