{
  "description": "Formulate a MILP for the integrated train rescheduling and speed management problem (TRSMP) under partial segment blockage. Variables: binary y_{i,r} for train i choosing route r (original or reroute), binary x_{i,j} for ordering of trains i and j on shared track segment s, continuous arrival time a_{i,k} and departure time d_{i,k} at station k, continuous travel time t_{i,s} on segment s, continuous speed v_{i,s} on segment s, binary z_{i,s} indicating use of accelerated profile. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay Σ_i (a_{i,last} - scheduled_arrival_i) and total energy Σ_i Σ_s (α_s * v_{i,s}^2 * t_{i,s}) where α_s is energy coefficient. Constraints: (1) each train selects exactly one route; (2) if reroute chosen, train uses opposite track on blocked segment during blockage window [B_start,B_end]; (3) flow: d_{i,k}=a_{i,k}+ dwell_i,k; (4) travel time relation: a_{i,k+1}=d_{i,k}+ t_{i,s(k)}; (5) travel time bounds: t_{i,s} >= L_s / v_max and <= L_s / v_min; (6) speed choice: v_{i,s}=v_normal if z_{i,s}=0 else v_accel; (7) ordering constraints on shared segment: for any two trains i,j using same track direction on segment s, a_{i,enter_s}+ t_{i,s} <= a_{j,enter_s} + M*(1-x_{i,j}) and vice versa; (8) blockage constraint: if segment s blocked on one track side during [B_start,B_end], trains on that side must either not use that side (y_{i,r}=original) or must be scheduled outside window: a_{i,enter_s} >= B_end or a_{i,enter_s}+t_{i,s} <= B_start; (9) non‑negative and binary domains."
}

