  "description": "Formulate a mixed-integer linear programming model for the integrated Train Rescheduling and Speed Management Problem (TRSMP) under partial segment blockages. Variables: binary route choice y_{i,t} (train i uses reroute on segment t), binary ordering x_{i,j,s} (train i precedes train j on shared segment s), continuous departure time D_i, arrival time A_i at each station, travel time T_{i,s} on segment s, speed level v_{i,s,k} (binary for speed option k on segment s). Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay Σ_i (A_i - scheduled arrival) and total energy Σ_i Σ_s Σ_k e_{s,k} * v_{i,s,k}. Constraints: (1) each train chooses either original or reroute on blocked segments; (2) travel time equals segment length divided by selected speed; (3) sequencing constraints using big-M to avoid conflicts on shared segments; (4) time window constraints for blocked segments; (5) dwell time minimum at stations; (6) speed limits; (7) binary and domain definitions."
