{
  "description": "Formulate a mixed-integer linear programming model for the integrated Train Rescheduling and Speed Management Problem (TRSMP) under partial segment blockage. Sets: T trains, S segments, N stations, K time intervals. Binary y_{t,s}=1 if train t uses segment s (including rerouting to opposite track). Binary z_{t,i}=1 if train t follows speed plan i (predefined plan with travel time tau_{t,i} and energy e_{t,i}). Continuous a_t departure time at origin, d_t arrival time at destination, and arrival time at station n: a_{t,n}, departure b_{t,n}. Parameters: scheduled times a^0_{t,n}, b^0_{t,n}, dwell time min D_{t,n}, max D_{t,n}, disruption window [T_start,T_end] on blocked segment s*. Travel time on segment s for plan i: tau_{t,i,s}. Energy e_{t,i}. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay sum_t (a_{t,N}-a^0_{t,N}) and total energy sum_{t,i} e_{t,i} z_{t,i}. Constraints: 1) Each train selects exactly one speed plan: sum_i z_{t,i}=1. 2) Timing consistency: a_{t,1}=a_t, b_{t,n}=a_{t,n}+D_{t,n} (if dwell). a_{t,n+1}=b_{t,n}+ sum_{s in path_{t}} tau_{t,i,s} where i is selected plan. 3) Conflict avoidance on each segment s and time interval k: sum_{t} y_{t,s} * x_{t,s,k} <= 1 where x_{t,s,k}=1 if train t occupies segment s during interval k (derived from a_{t,n}, travel times). 4) Rerouting feasibility: if segment s* is blocked during [T_start,T_end], then y_{t,s*}=0 for trains scheduled to occupy during that window; they may use opposite track s*_opp with binary variable r_{t}=1 if rerouted. 5) Binary linking: y_{t,s}=1 if segment s is in chosen route of train t (depends on r_t). 6) Delay limits: a_{t,N} - a^0_{t,N} <= L_max. 7) Energy calculation: total energy = sum_{t,i} e_{t,i} z_{t,i}. 8) Non‑negativity and binary domains.\n\nProvide the full set of equations, variable definitions, and assumptions."
}

