{
  "description": "Formulate a mixed-integer linear programming model for the integrated Train Rescheduling and Speed Management Problem (TRSMP) under partial track blockages. Variables: binary route choice r_{i}^{k} (train i uses alternative route k), binary order o_{ij} (train i precedes j on shared segment), continuous arrival times a_{i,s}, departure times d_{i,s} at stations s, binary speed segment selection v_{i,s,t} (train i uses speed level t on segment s), continuous energy consumption e_i. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay \n   \\sum_i (a_{i,final} - a_i^{0}) and total energy \\sum_i e_i. Constraints: (1) each train selects exactly one route; (2) for chosen route, travel time on each segment equals sum of segment times derived from speed levels: travel_{i,s}=\\sum_t v_{i,s,t} time_{s,t}. (3) speed level selection binary and sum to 1 per segment. (4) energy consumption computed as \\sum_{s,t} v_{i,s,t} energy_{s,t}. (5) precedence constraints on shared segments: if o_{ij}=1 then a_{j,start} >= d_{i,end}+ safety_gap. (6) disallow use of blocked segment during blockage window: a_{i,enter} >= block_end or d_{i,exit} <= block_start. (7) dwell time constraints at stations: d_{i,s} >= a_{i,s}+ dwell_min. (8) headway constraints between consecutive trains on same track. (9) binary order variables linked to arrival times: o_{ij}=1 iff a_{j,start} >= d_{i,end}+gap. (10) logical linking of route choice to order variables for bidirectional conflict. (11) domain constraints. Provide assumptions for parameters: scheduled arrival a_i^0, block window [B_s,B_e] per segment, speed levels t with known time and energy, safety gap, dwell minima, etc."
}

