{
  "description": "Formulate a MILP for integrated train rescheduling and speed management under partial segment blockage. Sets: T trains, S segments, N stations, time periods τ. Parameters: original departure d0_{t}, arrival a0_{t}, travel time base τ_{t,s}, disruption window [Δ_start_s, Δ_end_s] for blocked segment s, capacity cap_s (bidirectional), energy cost per unit speed e_s. Decision variables: x_{t,s}=1 if train t uses segment s (reroute), y_{t,τ}=1 if train t departs at time τ, z_{t,τ}=1 if arrives at time τ, v_{t,s} continuous speed on segment s, u_{t,τ} binary for acceleration/deceleration choice. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay Σ_t Σ_τ τ·(y_{t,τ}·τ - d0_t) + α·Σ_t Σ_s e_s·v_{t,s}·τ_{t,s}. Constraints: (1) each train selects exactly one departure time and one arrival time. (2) flow conservation: for each train t and segment sequence, x_{t,s}=1 implies continuity of times using travel time = length/v_{t,s}. (3) capacity: Σ_t x_{t,s} ≤ cap_s for each segment and time window, considering bidirectional conflict. (4) disruption: if segment s is blocked during [Δ_start_s,Δ_end_s], then x_{t,s}=0 for any τ within that window unless rerouted to opposite track (modeled by alternative segment s'). (5) speed limits: v_min ≤ v_{t,s} ≤ v_max. (6) acceleration/deceleration linking: if u_{t,τ}=1 then speed change Δv allowed. (7) dwell time at stations: arrival and departure times differ by minimum dwell d_min. (8) binary linking for rerouting: x_{t,s}+x_{t,s'} ≤1 for blocked segment and its opposite. Provide linearization for product of binary and continuous via big-M. Assumptions: time discretized, travel time linear in inverse speed approximated by piecewise linear segments."
