  "description": "Formulate a mixed-integer linear programming model for the integrated train rescheduling and speed management problem (TRSMP) under partial segment blockage. Sets: T trains, S stations, L track segments, P possible routes (original or rerouted). Parameters: scheduled arrival a0[t,s], departure d0[t,s]; disruption window [tw_start[l], tw_end[l]] for blocked segment l; travel time lower/upper bounds tau_min[t,l], tau_max[t,l]; energy cost per unit time e[t,l]; dwell time min dwell_min[t,s]; binary block indicator B[l]=1 if segment l blocked. Decision variables: binary x[t,p] route choice; continuous arrival A[t,s], departure D[t,s]; binary y[t,l] indicates train t uses segment l; continuous travel time tau[t,l]; binary z[t1,t2,l] ordering on shared segment l; binary r[t,l] reroute usage. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay Σ_t Σ_s (A[t,s]-a0[t,s]) plus total energy Σ_t Σ_l e[t,l]*tau[t,l]. Constraints: route selection Σ_p x[t,p]=1; link route to segment usage y[t,l]= Σ_p δ[p,l]*x[t,p]; timing: A[t,s]= D[t,prev(s)]+tau[t,l] for segment l between stations; tau bounds tau_min≤tau≤tau_max; if B[l]=1 then y[t,l]≤1-r[t,l] (must reroute or not use); dwell: D[t,s]≥A[t,s]+dwell_min; ordering: for any two trains sharing segment l, z[t1,t2,l]+z[t2,t1,l]=1 and D[t1,exit(l)]≤A[t2,entry(l)]+M(1- z[t1,t2,l]) etc. Ensure conflict-free: for shared segment l, either train1 passes before train2 or vice versa. Energy: tau[t,l] proportional to speed; linearized via piecewise segments if needed. Provide full MILP formulation."
}

