{
  "description": "Formulate a MILP for the integrated train rescheduling and speed management problem (TRSMP) under partial segment blockage disruptions. Variables: binary reroute decisions x_{t,s} for train t using alternative side of segment s; binary order variables y_{t1,t2,s} indicating if train t1 passes before t2 on shared segment s; continuous arrival times a_{t,i} at station i; departure times d_{t,i}; binary speed level selection u_{t,i,k} for speed profile segment i with level k (k=1..K) having travel time τ_{i,k} and energy e_{i,k}. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay Σ_t (a_{t,last} - scheduled_arrival_t) and total energy Σ_{t,i,k} e_{i,k} u_{t,i,k}. Constraints: (1) time feasibility a_{t,i}=d_{t,i-1}+ Σ_k τ_{i,k} u_{t,i,k}; (2) dwell time bounds d_{t,i} ≥ a_{t,i}+ minDwell_i, ≤ a_{t,i}+ maxDwell_i; (3) disruption availability: if segment s blocked during [T_start_s,T_end_s], then for any train t using that side x_{t,s}=0 unless reroute binary forces use opposite side; (4) conflict avoidance on shared segment: for any two trains t1,t2 using same side of segment s, y_{t1,t2,s}+ y_{t2,t1,s}=1 and a_{t1,exit_s} ≤ a_{t2,enter_s}+M(1- y_{t1,t2,s}); (5) each train chooses exactly one speed level per track section: Σ_k u_{t,i,k}=1; (6) binary x_{t,s} ties to route choice: if x_{t,s}=1 then train uses opposite side of s, else uses normal side. (7) start/end times respect disruption window: a_{t,enter_s} ≥ T_end_s if not rerouted. Assumptions: single line with two parallel tracks, blockage affects only one side, K discrete speed levels, big-M constant sufficiently large, scheduled times given, all trains must be served (no cancellation)."
}

