{
  "description": "Mixed-integer linear programming model for integrated train rescheduling and speed management under partial segment blockage. Sets: T trains, S segments, N stations, P time periods. Parameters: travel_time[t,s] nominal travel time, block_start[s], block_end[s] blockage window, capacity[s] tracks (1 or 2), energy_coeff[t] energy per unit speed, max_speed[t], min_speed[t], accel[t], decel[t]. Decision variables: x[t,s] binary if train t uses segment s (reroute), y[t,n] binary ordering between trains on same segment, a[t,n] arrival time of train t at station n, d[t,n] departure time, v[t,s] average speed on segment, e[t] energy consumption. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay Σ_t (a[t,final] - scheduled_arrival[t]) + λ Σ_t e[t]. Constraints: (1) flow: a[t,n+1] = d[t,n] + travel_time[t,s] * (nominal_speed/v[t,s]) ; (2) speed limits: min_speed ≤ v ≤ max_speed; (3) blockage: if segment s blocked during [block_start,block_end] then for any train using s, a[t,entry] ≥ block_end or d[t,exit] ≤ block_start; (4) binary routing: x[t,s] =1 if train uses opposite track during blockage; (5) conflict avoidance: for any two trains i,j sharing segment s, ordering variable y[i,j,s] ensures either d[i,exit] ≤ a[j,entry] or vice versa; (6) dwell time: d[t,n] ≥ a[t,n] + dwell_min; (7) energy: e[t] = Σ_s energy_coeff[t] * (v[t,s]^2) * travel_time[t,s]; (8) rescheduling limits: a[t,final] ≤ scheduled_arrival[t] + max_delay; (9) binary and nonnegativity.\n"
}

