{
  "description": "Formulate a mixed-integer linear programming model for the integrated Train Rescheduling and Speed Management Problem (TRSMP) under partial segment blockage. Sets: T trains, S segments, N stations, time horizon H discretized in intervals h. Parameters: travel time baseline tau_{t,s}, capacity C_s per direction, blockage window [B_s^{start}, B_s^{end}] on segment s for one direction, energy cost per unit speed e, max acceleration a_max, max deceleration d_max, max speed v_max, dwell time min D_{t,n}. Variables: binary x_{t,s}^{dir} indicates train t uses direction dir on segment s (0=original,1=routed opposite). Continuous arrival time A_{t,n}, departure time D_{t,n}. Continuous speed v_{t,s,h} on segment s at interval h. Binary y_{t,s,h} indicates train t occupies segment s at interval h. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay \n   sum_{t,n} (A_{t,n} - A_{t,n}^{sched}) plus total energy \n   sum_{t,s,h} e * v_{t,s,h} * y_{t,s,h}. Constraints: 1) Flow: D_{t,n}=A_{t,n}+D_{t,n}^{min}. 2) Travel time linking speeds: for each segment s traversed by t, sum_h (y_{t,s,h}*Δt) = travel time = sum_h (Δs / v_{t,s,h}). Linearize using piecewise speed intervals v_k with binary z_{t,s,k}. 3) Capacity: for each segment s and interval h, sum_t y_{t,s,h} <= C_s. 4) Blockage: if interval h lies within blockage window for direction dir, then y_{t,s,h}=0 for trains using that direction. 5) Rerouting: x_{t,s}^{dir}=1 only if allowed; if rerouted, direction opposite to original. 6) Conflict avoidance bidirectional: for opposite directions on same segment, sum_t y_{t,s,h} <= 1. 7) Acceleration/deceleration limits: v_{t,s,h+1} - v_{t,s,h} <= a_max*Δt, and v_{t,s,h} - v_{t,s,h+1} <= d_max*Δt. 8) Speed bounds: 0 <= v_{t,s,h} <= v_max * y_{t,s,h}. 9) Binary linking: y_{t,s,h} <= x_{t,s}^{dir} etc. Provide full linear equations.",
  "max_output_tokens": 2000
}

