{
  "description": "Formulate a MILP for integrated train rescheduling and speed management under partial segment blockage. Variables: binary route choice r_{i,s} (train i uses side s of segment), binary order o_{i,j} (train i precedes j on shared track), continuous arrival a_{i,k} and departure d_{i,k} at station k, continuous travel time t_{i,seg} on segment, continuous energy e_i. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay Σ_i (a_{i,last}-a^0_{i,last}) and total energy Σ_i e_i. Constraints: (1) each train chooses one side for blocked segment: Σ_s r_{i,s}=1. (2) if train uses side s, travel time on segment respects speed limits: t_{i,seg} ≥ L_seg / v_max_s * r_{i,s}. (3) speed-energy relation linearized: e_i ≥ α_i * t_{i,seg} + β_i * r_{i,s}. (4) precedence constraints on shared track: a_{j,entry} ≥ d_{i,exit} - M*(1-o_{i,j}) and a_{i,entry} ≥ d_{j,exit} - M*o_{i,j}. (5) dwell time bounds: d_{i,k} ≥ a_{i,k}+ dwell_min, d_{i,k} ≤ a_{i,k}+ dwell_max. (6) running time consistency: a_{i,k+1} = d_{i,k}+ t_{i,seg(k)}. (7) disruption window: for blocked side s*, no train may occupy segment during [T_start,T_end]: a_{i,entry} ≥ T_end or d_{i,exit} ≤ T_start if r_{i,s*}=1. (8) binary order variables defined for each pair of trains sharing a segment. (9) non‑negativity and binary domains. Assumptions: linear energy model, single blocked segment, fixed disruption window, known base timetable a^0. Provide full MILP formulation."
}

