{
  "description": "Formulate a MILP for integrated train rescheduling and speed management under partial segment blockage. Sets: trains i in I, segments s in S, time periods t in T. Parameters: original departure/arrival times a_i^orig, d_i^orig, travel time lower/upper bounds tau_{i,s}^{min}, tau_{i,s}^{max}, energy cost per unit time e_s, disruption window [t_start_s, t_end_s] for blocked segments, binary availability b_{s,t}=0 if segment s blocked at time t. Decision variables: departure time D_i, arrival time A_i, binary route choice r_{i,s}=1 if train i uses segment s (allow rerouting to opposite track), binary ordering o_{i,j,s,t}=1 if train i precedes train j on segment s at time t, continuous travel time on segment x_{i,s} >=0, binary speed level v_{i,s,k} for k in K speed levels, energy consumption E_i. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay sum_i (A_i - a_i^orig) + total energy sum_i E_i. Constraints: (1) timing: D_i >= d_i^orig, A_i >= a_i^orig. (2) segment travel time: tau_{i,s}^{min} <= x_{i,s} <= tau_{i,s}^{max}. (3) linking travel times to departure/arrival: D_i + sum_{s before s'} x_{i,s} = arrival at next station, etc. (4) blockage: if b_{s,t}=0 then no train can occupy segment s at time t: sum_i o_{i,*,s,t} <= 0. (5) capacity: at most one train on a segment at a time: sum_i o_{i,*,s,t} <= 1. (6) ordering consistency: o_{i,j,s,t}+o_{j,i,s,t}=1 for any two trains sharing segment s at overlapping times. (7) rerouting: r_{i,s}=1 only if segment s is available or opposite track is used; binary linking with blockage. (8) speed-energy: E_i = sum_{s} sum_{k} e_s * v_{i,s,k} * x_{i,s}. (9) speed level selection: sum_k v_{i,s,k}=1 for each i,s. (10) linking travel time to speed level: x_{i,s} = L_s / v_{k} where L_s length of segment, v_k speed of level k (linearized via big-M). (11) binary domain constraints. Assumptions: linearization of speed-energy relationship, big-M constants M large enough, time discretized into periods T.\n"
}

