{
  "description": "Formulate an integrated train rescheduling and speed management problem (TRSMP) for high-speed railway with partial segment blockages. Variables: binary y_{i,k} selecting speed plan k for train i; continuous t_{i,s} arrival time of train i at station s; continuous v_{i,s}^{acc}, v_{i,s}^{dec} acceleration/deceleration rates; binary z_{i,j,s} ordering of conflicting trains i and j at station s. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay (t_{i,last}-scheduled) and total energy consumption (sum over trains and segments of energy proportional to acceleration and speed). Constraints: each train selects exactly one speed plan; arrival times follow travel time from selected plan: t_{i,s+1}=t_{i,s}+travel_{i,k,s} where travel_{i,k,s} derived from speed plan k. Conflict avoidance on shared segment during disruption: if trains i and j use same segment during disruption window, ordering binary ensures non-overlap: t_{i,enter}+duration <= t_{j,enter} + M(1-z_{i,j}); and similarly opposite. Rerouting: binary r_{i,s} indicates if train i uses opposite track on segment s within disruption window; capacity constraints ensure at most one train uses opposite side per time. Energy consumption: E_i = sum_s (a_i * v_{i,s}^{acc}^2 + b_i * v_{i,s}^{dec}^2). Linearize by using precomputed energy per plan: energy_{i,k}. Then energy = sum_k energy_{i,k} * y_{i,k}. Delay: d_i = t_{i,last} - scheduled_last_i. Objective: min sum_i (w1 * d_i + w2 * sum_k energy_{i,k} * y_{i,k}). Assumptions: travel times and energy per plan are known constants; M is big M; disruption window [T_start,T_end] given."
}

