{
  "description": "MILP model for integrated train rescheduling and speed management under partial segment blockage. Sets: T trains, S stations, L line segments, P possible speed plans for each train. Parameters: travel time baseline a_{t,l}, energy e_{p} for plan p, disruption window [U_l, V_l] for blocked segment l, capacity C_l per time unit, dwell time min d_min. Decision variables: x_{t,s} arrival time of train t at station s (continuous), y_{t,l} binary if train t uses segment l (1 if uses normal direction, 0 if rerouted opposite), z_{t,p} binary selecting speed plan p for train t, w_{t,l,k} binary if train t occupies segment l at time interval k. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay Σ_t (x_{t,final} - scheduled_arrival_t) + α Σ_t Σ_p e_p*z_{t,p}. Constraints: (1) timing continuity: x_{t,s+1} >= x_{t,s} + Σ_p travel_time_{p,l}*z_{t,p} for segment l between s and s+1. (2) dwell time: x_{t,s} - departure_{t,s-1} >= d_min. (3) exactly one speed plan: Σ_p z_{t,p}=1. (4) segment usage: y_{t,l}=1 implies w_{t,l,k}=0 for k in disruption window, otherwise w_{t,l,k}=1 if train passes. (5) capacity: Σ_t w_{t,l,k} <= C_l for all l,k. (6) rerouting binary consistency: if segment blocked y_{t,l}=0 then train must use opposite direction alternative segment l' with y_{t,l'}=1. (7) conflict avoidance bidirectional: for any two trains t!=t' sharing opposite directions on same segment at same interval, w_{t,l,k}+w_{t',l,k} <=1. (8) arrival/departure windows: x_{t,s} within [scheduled_lower, scheduled_upper]. (9) variables bounds: x >=0, z binary, y binary, w binary."
}

