  "description": "Formulate a mixed-integer linear programming model for the integrated train rescheduling and speed management problem (TRSMP) under partial segment blockage. Set of trains T, set of segments S, time horizon discretized into periods k in K. Decision variables: x_{t,s,k} binary if train t uses segment s in period k (routing and rerouting); y_{t,k} continuous arrival time of train t at end of period k; v_{t,k} continuous speed of train t in period k; a_{t,k} binary acceleration/deceleration decision. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay (arrival minus original schedule) and total energy consumption (proportional to v^2 * a). Constraints: (1) flow conservation for each train across segments; (2) capacity: sum_{t} x_{t,s,k} <= 1 for each segment s and period k (bidirectional conflict); (3) blockage: x_{t,s,k}=0 for blocked segment s during its disruption window; (4) timing: y_{t,k+1}= y_{t,k}+ L_s / v_{t,k} where L_s length of segment s traversed if x_{t,s,k}=1; linearized using big-M; (5) speed limits: v_min <= v_{t,k} <= v_max; (6) acceleration/deceleration limits linking a_{t,k} and speed change; (7) dwell time at stations: y_{t,arrival}+dwell <= y_{t,departure}; (8) original schedule adherence: delay_t = y_{t,final} - scheduled_arrival_t; (9) binary variables for rerouting decision r_t (0 original track,1 opposite track). Energy consumption approximated as e_{t,k}= alpha * v_{t,k}^2 + beta * a_{t,k}. Linearize quadratic term by piecewise linear approximation with additional variables. Provide full MILP formulation."
}

