{
  "description": "Generate MILP for integrated train rescheduling and speed management under partial segment blockage. Variables: binary route choice y_{i,t} (train i uses reroute on segment s), binary order x_{i,j,s} (train i precedes j on segment s), continuous arrival a_{i,n}, departure d_{i,n} at station n, travel time τ_{i,s} on segment s, speed level v_{i,s} (discrete levels). Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay Σ_i (a_{i,last}- scheduled_i) and energy consumption Σ_i Σ_s e(v_{i,s})·τ_{i,s}. Constraints: sequence consistency a_{i,n+1}=d_{i,n}+τ_{i,segment(i,n)}; dwell time bounds; speed limits per segment; energy model linearized; blockage: if segment s blocked in window [T_start,T_end] then y_{i,s}=1 forces opposite track usage with capacity; capacity: for any segment s and time t, at most one train in each direction, modeled by ordering binaries x_{i,j,s} and time separation Δ. Conflict‑free: if x_{i,j,s}=1 then a_{i,enter_s}+τ_{i,s} ≤ a_{j,enter_s}. Bidirectional conflict: if trains opposite direction share same physical track then sum of binaries ≤1. Binary routing: y_{i,s}=0 means normal track, y_{i,s}=1 uses opposite track (available only if not blocked). Provide all sets, parameters, assumptions."
}

