{
  "description": "Formulate a mixed-integer linear programming model for the integrated train rescheduling and speed management problem (TRSMP) under partial segment blockage. Sets: T trains, S segments, N stations, time horizon H discretized in intervals h. Parameters: original arrival a_{t,s}, departure d_{t,s}, travel time tau_{t,s} (baseline), disruption window [u_s, v_s] for blocked segment s, capacity cap_s (max trains per direction), energy cost coeff e_{t,s} per unit time at speed level. Decision variables: x_{t,s,h} binary if train t occupies segment s during interval h, y_{t,s,h} binary direction (0/1), p_{t,s,h} continuous speed level, arr_{t,n} continuous arrival time at station n, dep_{t,n} departure time, z_{t,order} binary ordering between conflicting trains, r_{t,s} binary reroute (use opposite track). Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay and energy consumption. Constraints: (1) flow conservation linking segment occupation to arrivals/departures, (2) time feasibility arr/dep respecting travel times tau adjusted by speed p, (3) blockage: if h in [u_s,v_s] then x_{t,s,h}=0 unless reroute r_{t,s}=1, (4) capacity: sum_{t} x_{t,s,h} <= cap_s for each direction, (5) conflict avoidance: for any two trains t1,t2 on same segment opposite directions, enforce ordering via z variables, (6) speed limits: p_{t,s,h} between min and max, (7) energy: energy_{t}=sum e_{t,s} * p_{t,s,h} * delta_h, (8) binary linking: r_{t,s}=1 implies using opposite direction y, (9) dwell time constraints at stations, (10) cancellation: optional binary c_t if train cancelled, then no occupancy. Provide equations."
}

