{
  "description": "Formulate a MILP for integrated train rescheduling and speed management under partial segment blockage. Sets: T trains, S stations, L line segments, K time intervals. Binary y_{t,l}=1 if train t uses segment l (original or opposite direction) during disruption window. Binary z_{t1,t2,l}=1 if train t1 precedes t2 on shared segment l. Continuous variables: a_{t,s} arrival time of train t at station s, d_{t,s} departure time, v_{t,l,k} speed of train t on segment l during interval k, tau_{t,l,k} travel time on segment l in interval k. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay (a_{t,last}- scheduled arrival) and total energy consumption (sum over t,l,k of energy coefficient e_{l} * v_{t,l,k}^2 * tau_{t,l,k}). Constraints: (1) timing continuity: d_{t,s}=a_{t,s}+ dwell_t_s. (2) travel time linking speeds: tau_{t,l,k}= length_l / v_{t,l,k} if segment l traversed in interval k, else 0. (3) arrival propagation: a_{t,s+1}=d_{t,s}+ sum_k tau_{t,l(s),k}. (4) speed limits: v_min_l <= v_{t,l,k} <= v_max_l * y_{t,l}. (5) binary routing: for each train t, sum_l y_{t,l}= number of segments in its path; if disruption, allow opposite direction segment usage with penalty. (6) conflict avoidance: for any two trains t1,t2 sharing segment l, either z_{t1,t2,l}=1 and d_{t1,exit_l} <= a_{t2,enter_l} or opposite; modeled with big-M: a_{t2,enter_l} >= d_{t1,exit_l} - M*(1-z_{t1,t2,l}) and a_{t1,enter_l} >= d_{t2,exit_l} - M*z_{t1,t2,l}. (7) disruption window: y_{t,l}=0 for blocked direction during time window unless opposite direction used. (8) cancellation: binary c_t=1 if train t cancelled; then a_{t,last}=d_{t,last}=0 and no speed variables. (9) total number of cancellations limited. (10) reordering: ordering variables o_{t1,t2}=1 if t1 before t2 on shared segment, linked to z variables. Provide big-M values. Assumptions: discrete time intervals, linearized energy as quadratic approximated by piecewise linear segments, big-M sufficiently large."
}

