{
  "description": "Create a MILP model for integrated train rescheduling and speed management under partial segment blockage. Sets: T trains, S segments, N stations, P possible speed plans per train. Parameters: original arrival a_i^0, departure d_i^0, travel time t_{i,s}^0, disruption window [u_s, v_s] for blocked segment s, energy cost e_{i,p} for plan p, binary conflict indicator c_{i,j,s} if trains i and j use same segment s in opposite directions. Decision variables: binary x_{i,p} =1 if train i uses speed plan p; continuous arrival A_i, departure D_i at each station; binary y_{i,s}=1 if train i uses segment s (including rerouting); binary z_{i,j,s}=1 if conflict resolved by ordering. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay sum_i (A_i - a_i^0) + total energy sum_{i,p} e_{i,p} x_{i,p}. Constraints: each train selects exactly one plan; timing consistency A_i + travel_{i,s,p} <= A_j for downstream; segment capacity: for any segment s and time t, at most one train in each direction unless ordering variable resolves; disruption: if segment s blocked in [u_s,v_s], then y_{i,s}=0 for any train i during that window unless rerouted (alternative segment usage). Speed plan linking: travel time on segment s for train i equals sum_p tau_{i,s,p} x_{i,p}. Energy linking: energy = sum_p e_{i,p} x_{i,p}. Conflict ordering: z_{i,j,s}+z_{j,i,s}=1 if both use s opposite directions, and enforce A_i + tau <= A_j or vice versa based on order. Binary variables for rerouting r_i_s =1 if train i reroutes around blocked segment. Ensure at most one reroute per train. Provide all equations."
}

