{
  "description": "Formulate a MILP for integrated train rescheduling and speed management under partial segment blockage. Variables: binary route choice r_{i,s} (train i uses side s of segment), binary ordering o_{i,j,s} (train i precedes j on side s), continuous arrival times a_{i,k}, departure times d_{i,k} at stations k, continuous travel times t_{i,seg} on segments, binary speed profile selection p_{i,seg,m} (profile m). Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay Σ_i (a_{i,last}-a_i^scheduled) and energy consumption Σ_i Σ_seg Σ_m e_{m} * p_{i,seg,m}. Constraints: each train chooses one side per blocked segment, flow conservation a_{i,k}+dwell_i ≤ d_{i,k}, d_{i,k}+t_{i,seg}=a_{i,next}, speed profile linking travel time t_{i,seg}=L_seg/v_m * p_{i,seg,m}, exactly one profile per segment, ordering constraints to avoid conflicts on same side: if o_{i,j,s}=1 then a_{i,exit}+safety ≤ a_{j,entry}, and mutual exclusivity o_{i,j,s}+o_{j,i,s}=1 for trains sharing side. Capacity: at most C trains on side s at any time. Binary variables for cancellation c_i with big-M linking to zero travel times. Assumptions: fixed dwell times, known segment lengths, set of discrete speed profiles with known energy per profile. Provide full MILP equations."
}

