{
  "description": "Create a MILP model for integrated train rescheduling and speed management under partial segment blockage. Variables: binary x_{i,r} for train i selecting speed plan r, binary y_{i,j,s} for ordering of trains i and j on shared segment s, continuous arrival a_{i,n}, departure d_{i,n} at stations n, continuous travel time t_{i,s} on segment s, binary z_{i,s} for rerouting on opposite track in disruption window. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay \n    sum_i (a_{i,last} - scheduled_arrival_i) and total energy consumption sum_{i,r} E_{i,r} x_{i,r}. Constraints: each train selects exactly one speed plan; arrival/departure consistency a_{i,n}+ dwell <= d_{i,n}; travel time t_{i,s}= d_{i,n} - a_{i,prev}; if segment s is blocked during window [T_start,T_end], then either train uses opposite track (z_{i,s}=1) within that window or cannot occupy blocked side; ordering constraints: for any two trains i,j sharing segment s, y_{i,j,s}+y_{j,i,s}=1 and if y_{i,j,s}=1 then a_{i,enter_s}+ safety <= a_{j,enter_s}; rerouting capacity: sum_i z_{i,s} <= capacity_opposite_s; speed plan feasibility: t_{i,s} within min/max bounds of plan r selected; energy consumption E_{i,r} given per plan. Also ensure binary variables domain and large-M linking."
}

