{
  "description": "Formulate a mixed-integer linear programming model for the integrated train rescheduling and speed management problem (TRSMP) under partial segment blockage. Sets: T trains, S segments, N stations, K time intervals. Parameters: original departure/arrival times, travel time lower/upper bounds, disruption window [u_s, v_s] for blocked segment s, energy cost per unit speed change, capacity of segment (1 train per direction). Decision variables: x_{t,s}=1 if train t uses segment s (original direction), y_{t,s}=1 if rerouted to opposite direction, a_{t,n}=actual arrival time at station n, d_{t,n}=departure time, v_{t,k}=average speed of train t in interval k, z_{t,k}=1 if train t is active in interval k. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay Σ_t (a_{t,last}-a^0_{t,last}) and total energy Σ_t Σ_k c_k * v_{t,k}. Constraints: (1) each train follows a path: for each segment s on its route, x_{t,s}+y_{t,s}=1. (2) Rerouting only allowed on blocked segment during disruption window: y_{t,s} ≤ 1 if s is blocked and time window overlaps, else y_{t,s}=0. (3) Flow continuity: departure from station n equals arrival plus dwell time. (4) Travel time linking speed and time: for each segment s traversed in interval k, travel time = length_s / v_{t,k} and must lie within bounds. (5) Capacity: for any segment s and any time interval k, sum_t (x_{t,s}*z_{t,k}+ y_{t,s}*z_{t,k}) ≤ 1 (bidirectional conflict). (6) Time feasibility: a_{t,n+1} ≥ d_{t,n}+ travel_time_{t,s}. (7) Delay variables defined as Δ_t = a_{t,last}-a^0_{t,last}. (8) Binary variables definitions. Provide linearization for product x_{t,s}*z_{t,k} using auxiliary w_{t,s,k} ≤ x_{t,s}, w_{t,s,k} ≤ z_{t,k}, w_{t,s,k} ≥ x_{t,s}+z_{t,k}-1. Similarly for y. Return the full set of equations."
}

