{
  "description": "Create a MILP model for integrated train rescheduling and speed management under partial segment blockage. Sets: T trains, S segments, N stations, I time intervals. Parameters: travel time base tt_{t,s}, capacity cap_s, blockage start/break end B_start_s, B_end_s, energy cost per speed e_v, max speed v_max, min speed v_min, acceleration a_max, deceleration d_max, dwell time min dwell_{t,n}. Decision variables: x_{t,s,i}=binary if train t uses segment s in interval i, y_{t,n}=arrival time of train t at station n (continuous), z_{t,s,i}=binary reroute decision (use opposite track), v_{t,i}=continuous speed of train t in interval i, a_{t,i}=continuous accel/decel, u_{t}=binary cancel train. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay 
 sum_{t,n} (y_{t,n}- scheduled_{t,n}) plus total energy sum_{t,i} e_v * v_{t,i}*Δt. Constraints: 1) flow: for each train and segment, if segment traversed then continuity of arrival times via speed: y_{t, end(s)} >= y_{t, start(s)} + (len_s / v_{t,i}) . 2) capacity: sum_{t} x_{t,s,i} <= cap_s for all s,i not in blockage window; during blockage, only opposite track allowed via z. 3) speed limits: v_min <= v_{t,i} <= v_max, accel limits: a_{t,i}= (v_{t,i}-v_{t,i-1})/Δt, -d_max <= a_{t,i} <= a_max. 4) blockage: x_{t,s,i}=0 for i in [B_start_s, B_end_s] unless z_{t,s,i}=1 (reroute). 5) dwell time: y_{t, n+1} - y_{t,n} >= dwell_{t,n}. 6) ordering: for trains moving same direction on same track, ensure headway H: y_{t2, n} >= y_{t1, n}+H if x_{t1,s,i}=x_{t2,s,i}=1 and t1 precedes t2. 7) binary linking: z_{t,s,i} <=1 - x_{t,s,i}. 8) cancellation: if u_t=1 then all variables for train t are zero and no penalty for delay but large cancellation penalty in objective.
Assumptions: Time discretized into equal intervals Δt, each train assigned a single speed per interval, segment length known, opposite track capacity same as normal.
Return the model equations."
}

