{
  "description": "Formulate an integrated train rescheduling and speed management MILP for high-speed railway disruptions caused by partial segment blockages. Sets: T trains, S stations, L track segments (bidirectional), P possible routes for each train (original or rerouted). Parameters: travel time base t_{i,j} for train i on segment j, energy consumption e_{i,j} per unit time, disruption window [a_j,b_j] for blocked segment j, capacity C_j for each segment (max one train per direction at a time). Decision variables: x_{i,p}=1 if train i chooses route p, y_{i,j}=1 if train i uses segment j, start time s_i, arrival time at station k a_{i,k}, departure time d_{i,k}, binary z_{i,j}=1 if train i traverses segment j during disruption window, continuous speed v_{i,j} on segment j. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay Σ_i (a_{i,last}- scheduled arrival) plus total energy Σ_i Σ_j e_{i,j} * (travel time on segment j). Constraints: each train selects exactly one route, segment usage consistency, time feasibility a_{i,k}+ dwell ≤ d_{i,k}, travel time relation d_{i,k}+ t_{i,j}= a_{i,k+1} adjusted by speed v, speed limits v_min ≤ v_{i,j} ≤ v_max, if segment j is blocked during [a_j,b_j] then z_{i,j}=1 forces either reroute (y_{i,j}=0) or speed adjustment to avoid window, capacity: sum_i y_{i,j} ≤ C_j for each time slice, binary linking y and x, and big-M for conflict avoidance between opposite directions on shared track. Provide all equations."
}

