{
  "description": "Formulate a MILP for integrated train rescheduling and speed management under partial segment blockage. Variables: binary route choice r_{i,s} (train i uses side s of segment), binary order o_{i,j} (train i precedes j on shared track), continuous arrival a_{i,k} and departure d_{i,k} at station k, continuous travel time t_{i,seg} on segment, speed v_{i,seg}. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay Σ_i (a_{i,last}- scheduled_i) and energy consumption Σ_i Σ_seg (α v_{i,seg}^2 + β v_{i,seg}) . Constraints: (1) each train chooses exactly one side on blocked segment; (2) flow conservation a_{i,k}+ dwell = d_{i,k}; d_{i,k}+ travel = a_{i,k+1}; (3) travel time linked to speed: t_{i,seg}= length_seg / v_{i,seg}; (4) speed bounds; (5) capacity: for any two trains on same side, ordering binary o_{i,j} ensures no overlap: d_{i,enter}+ safety ≤ a_{j,enter} if o_{i,j}=1, else opposite; (6) disruption window: trains cannot occupy blocked side during [T_start,T_end]; (7) rerouting allowed: if blocked side unavailable, r_{i,blocked}=0 forces use opposite side; (8) binary ordering consistency o_{i,j}+o_{j,i}=1 for trains sharing side; (9) optional cancellation binary c_i with big-M linking to zero travel. Assumptions: linearization of speed-energy via piecewise linear segments, big-M constants M. Provide full MILP equations."
}

