{
  "description": "Formulate a MILP for integrated train rescheduling and speed management under partial segment blockage. Sets: trains i in I, segments s in S, time periods t in T. Parameters: original departure/arrival times a_i^orig, d_i^orig, disruption window [t_start, t_end] on blocked segment s*. Travel time lower/upper bounds tau_min_{i,s}, tau_max_{i,s}. Energy cost per unit time e_i. Binary x_{i,s}=1 if train i uses segment s (routing decision, allows opposite track usage during blockage). Binary y_{i,t}=1 if train i departs at time t (retiming). Continuous v_{i,s}= speed on segment s. Variables: departure time D_i, arrival time A_i, segment traversal start/finish times start_{i,s}, end_{i,s}. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay (A_i - a_i^orig) and energy consumption sum_i sum_s e_i * v_{i,s} * (end_{i,s}-start_{i,s}). Constraints: 1) Routing: if segment s is blocked and time window overlaps, then x_{i,s}=1 only if train uses opposite track. 2) Time continuity: start_{i,s}=end_{i,prev(s)}. 3) Travel time bounds: tau_min_{i,s} <= end_{i,s}-start_{i,s} <= tau_max_{i,s}. 4) Speed limits: v_min <= v_{i,s} <= v_max. 5) Conflict avoidance: for any two trains i,j on same track direction on segment s, their traversal intervals cannot overlap: end_{i,s} <= start_{j,s} + M*(1 - z_{i,j,s}) and end_{j,s} <= start_{i,s} + M*z_{i,j,s}, with binary z_{i,j,s}. 6) Bidirectional conflict on shared track during blockage: similar constraints using x variables. 7) D_i = sum_t t*y_{i,t}. 8) Departure within allowed window: D_i >= d_i^orig - L_delay, D_i <= d_i^orig + U_delay. 9) Arrival consistency: A_i = D_i + sum_s (end_{i,s}-start_{i,s}). 10) Dwell time at stations: enforce minimum dwell. 11) Cancellation option: binary c_i, if cancelled then D_i and A_i not counted in objective.\n"
}

