{
  "description": "Formulate a MILP for integrated train rescheduling and speed management under partial segment blockage. Sets: trains i in I, segments s in S, time periods t in T. Parameters: original departure/arrival times a_i^0, d_i^0, travel time lower/upper bounds tau_{i,s}^{min}, tau_{i,s}^{max}, energy cost per unit time e_s, disruption window [t_start, t_end] on blocked segment s*. Binary x_{i,s}=1 if train i uses segment s (original direction), y_{i,s}=1 if rerouted to opposite track on blocked segment. Continuous variables: departure time D_i, arrival time A_i, segment traversal start time u_{i,s}, traversal duration v_{i,s}. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay sum_i (A_i - a_i^0) + lambda * total energy sum_{i,s} e_s * v_{i,s}. Constraints: 1) departure/arrival consistency D_i + sum_s v_{i,s} = A_i. 2) traversal time bounds tau_{i,s}^{min} <= v_{i,s} <= tau_{i,s}^{max}. 3) sequencing on each segment: for any two trains i,k using same direction x_{i,s}=x_{k,s}=1, enforce either u_{i,s}+v_{i,s} <= u_{k,s} or u_{k,s}+v_{k,s} <= u_{i,s} using big-M and binary z_{i,k,s}. 4) bidirectional conflict on blocked segment s*: if train i uses opposite track y_{i,s*}=1 then it occupies same physical resource, so similar sequencing constraints with trains using original direction on that segment. 5) disruption window: if train i traverses blocked segment s* (x_{i,s*}=1) then its traversal must be outside [t_start,t_end]: u_{i,s*} >= t_end or u_{i,s*}+v_{i,s*} <= t_start, modeled with binary w_{i}. 6) rerouting decision: y_{i,s*}=1 - x_{i,s*}. 7) dwell time at stations (optional) d_i^{min} <= D_i - A_{prev(i)} <= d_i^{max}. 8) binary domain for x,y,z,w. Assumptions: single track per direction, linear energy proportional to traversal time, fixed disruption window, all trains must be scheduled."
}

