{
  "description": "Formulate a MILP for integrated train rescheduling and speed management under partial segment blockage. Sets: T trains, S segments, N stations, time periods tau. Parameters: original arrival a0[t,n], departure d0[t,n]; disruption window [t_start,s_end]; capacity cap[s]; travel time min_travel[t,s]; energy coeff e[t,s]; binary blockage B[s]=1 if segment blocked. Decision variables: x[t,n] arrival time, y[t,n] departure time (continuous); z[t,s] binary if train t uses segment s (including possible reroute to opposite track); v[t,s,τ] binary if train t traverses segment s at time τ; p[t,s,τ] continuous speed (km/h) on segment s at time τ. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay Σ_t Σ_n (x[t,n]-a0[t,n]) plus total energy Σ_t Σ_s Σ_τ e[t,s]*p[t,s,τ]. Constraints: 1) Time consistency: y[t,n] = x[t,n] + dwell[t,n]; 2) Travel time linking: x[t,n+1] >= y[t,n] + Σ_s∈path(t,n) Σ_τ v[t,s,τ]*Δτ where Δτ is period length, ensuring speed respects min travel: Σ_τ v[t,s,τ]*Δτ >= min_travel[t,s]*z[t,s]; 3) Capacity: Σ_t v[t,s,τ] <= cap[s] for all s,τ; 4) Blockage: v[t,s,τ]=0 for τ in disruption window if B[s]=1; 5) Rerouting: if segment s blocked, train may use opposite track s' with binary z[t,s']; ensure only one route: Σ_s z[t,s]=1 for each required segment; 6) Speed limits: p[t,s,τ] <= vmax[s]*v[t,s,τ]; p[t,s,τ] >= vmin[s]*v[t,s,τ]; 7) Energy calculation: energy = Σ e[t,s]*p[t,s,τ]*Δτ; 8) Binary definitions: z,t,s ∈{0,1}, v,t,s,τ ∈{0,1}. Assumptions: time discretized, dwell times known, speed linearized, energy proportional to speed."
}

