{
  "description": "Formulate a MILP for the integrated Train Rescheduling and Speed Management Problem (TRSMP) under partial segment blockage. Variables: binary route choice r_{i,s} for train i using side s (0/1), binary ordering o_{i,j,s} if train i precedes j on side s, continuous departure time d_i, arrival time a_i, travel time t_{i,k} on segment k, speed v_{i,k}. Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay Σ_i (a_i - scheduled_arrival_i) and energy consumption Σ_i Σ_k (c1 * v_{i,k}^2 + c2 * (v_{i,k} - v_{i,k-1})^2). Constraints: each train chooses one side, time windows respecting disruption (if segment blocked on side s during [T_start,T_end], then cannot traverse), sequencing constraints using big-M, travel time = length / v, speed limits, acceleration limits, dwell time minimum, flow conservation, and binary ordering consistency. Provide full equations and assumptions."
}

